The android.jar stubs throw at runtime. I need to fake `android.content.Context` and `ContextWrapper` and `SharedPreferences` too. Let me create fake versions in the fakelib (which is first on the classpath).

Fake Context: an abstract class with the needed methods. Since Settings only calls `context.getSharedPreferences(...)` and `context.applicationContext`, I can write:

```java
package android.content;
public class Context {
    public Context() {}
    public Context getApplicationContext() { return this; }
    public SharedPreferences getSharedPreferences(String name, int mode) { return null; }
}
public class ContextWrapper extends Context {
    private final Context base;
    public ContextWrapper(Context base) { this.base = base; }
    @Override public SharedPreferences getSharedPreferences(String n, int m) { return base != null ? base.getSharedPreferences(n,m) : null; }
}
```

And SharedPreferences is an interface — I can keep the real interface from android.jar (interfaces don't throw). Actually the interface is fine to use from android.jar since it's just an interface. But my FakePrefs implements the real android.content.SharedPreferences interface → loading the interface from android.jar is fine (interfaces don't have stub bodies... they may have default methods with `throw new RuntimeException("Stub!")`, but I don't use defaults).

