Now fix the lexicon to have two distinct sets, and update the call sites.

Call sites:
- `joinPieces` uses `GuardLexicon.isKnownCyrillic(...)` → should use `captionWords` (ru_valid ≈ _KNOWN_WORDS + _CONFUSION_SEEDS)
- `rescueNarrowGap` uses `GuardLexicon.isKnown(...)` → `guardWords` (ru ∪ en)
- `restoreKnownWords` uses `GuardLexicon.KNOWN.contains(low)` → `knownWords` (exactly `_KNOWN_WORDS`)
- `dpSplitOnKnown` uses `GuardLexicon.KNOWN.contains(...)` → `knownWords`

Let me restructure GuardLexicon:
```kotlin
private object GuardLexicon {
    private val knownWords: Set<String> = setOf(...)
    private val enTech: Set<String> = setOf(...)
    private val confusionSeeds: Set<String> = setOf(...)

    /** `_KNOWN_WORDS` — используется restore_known_words и его DP-сегментация. */
    val CAPTION: Set<String> = knownWords

    /** Аналог `_ru_valid_words()` без JSON-урожая. */
    val RU: Set<String> = knownWords + confusionSeeds

    /** Аналог `_ru_valid_words() ∪ _en_valid_words()` без JSON-урожая. */
    val GUARD: Set<String> = RU + enTech
}
```

Then:
- joinPieces: `GuardLexicon.RU.contains(core.lowercase())`
- rescueNarrowGap: `GuardLexicon.GUARD.contains(token.lowercase())`
- restoreKnownWords / dpSplitOnKnown: `GuardLexicon.CAPTION.contains(...)`

Let me make the edits.

